<title>CANADA: Ford Canada union says no talks before GM deal.</title>
<headline>Ford Canada union says no talks before GM deal.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The union representing workers at Ford Motors Co's Canadian unit said it will not move contract talks to Ford from General Motors Corp's Canadian unit until a tentative agreement is in place at GM.</p>
<p>&quot;It is the position of the Ford bargaining council that we not set a strike deadline until such time as they reach a tentative settlement at General Motors,&quot; said Bob Such, chairman of the Canadian Auto Worker union's master bargaining committee at Ford.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't feel it would be appropriate for us to move into Ford when the GM workers are on strike.&quot;</p>
</text>
